This agreement is between you and @PUBLISHER@ ("Provider") and covers the @NAME_EN@ software, including its installer, input method, spacing engine, data files and documentation (the "Software"). By installing or using the Software you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not install it, or remove it if already installed. If the Korean and English versions differ, the Korean version prevails.

1. License. Provider grants you a free, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to install and use the Software for personal and work purposes on computers you own or control, with no limit on the number of computers.

2. Restrictions. Except as expressly permitted by law or by the licenses of the third-party components in section 5, you may not: (a) sell, rent or lease the Software or include it in a paid product or service; (b) redistribute it anywhere other than Provider's official download location without written permission (linking to that location is fine); (c) modify it or distribute works derived from it; or (d) remove or alter its copyright notices, this agreement or the third-party notices.

3. Early version. This is an early (pre-1.0) version. Features may change or be removed, it may contain errors, and it may not work correctly in some applications. Check the results when writing important documents.

4. Privacy. The Software does not log or transmit what you type. All processing happens on your computer. The Windows version does not connect to the network. Unless you turn these off in Settings, the macOS version connects to Provider's download server (dl.sebansios.com) only to fetch, once a day, an update-information file to check for a new version, and to download, once, the full version of its candidate-window font when a hanja character missing from the bundled font first appears; it also downloads a new version's installer when you choose to install it. These requests contain nothing you type and no device information; as with any download, only connection information such as your IP address reaches the server. A new version is installed only if you choose to install it. Only your settings, the words you register and, while the option is on, the few words around spacing boundaries you correct by hand are stored locally; you can delete them in Settings at any time. If you choose a wordbook sync folder, the Software writes a wordbook file with your registered words and remembered spacing to that folder and reads other devices' wordbook files from it. Provider never receives these files; any service that syncs the folder is governed by its own terms.

5. Third-party components. The Software includes open-source components such as the Kiwi morphological analyzer (GNU LGPL). Each component is governed by its own license, which prevails over this agreement for that component; nothing here limits the rights those licenses grant you. In particular you may modify or replace the LGPL-licensed libraries and reverse engineer the Software to the extent needed to debug such modifications. The list of components and their full license texts are in the Licenses folder installed with the Software (on macOS, Contents/Resources/Licenses inside the app; on Windows, Licenses in the installation folder) and the THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES document in it. The Microsoft redistributable runtimes included in the Windows version (the Visual C++ Runtime and the Universal C Runtime) are subject to Microsoft's license terms; except as permitted by law, you may not modify, reverse engineer or separately distribute them.

6. Ownership. Provider or the respective rights holders retain all copyright and other intellectual property rights in the Software. This agreement grants a license to use it and does not transfer ownership.

7. No warranty. The Software is provided free of charge and "as is". To the maximum extent permitted by law, Provider makes no warranty of any kind, express or implied, including the accuracy of spacing or conversion results, fitness for a particular purpose and freedom from errors.

8. Limitation of liability. To the maximum extent permitted by law, Provider is not liable for any damages arising from the use of or inability to use the Software, except for damages caused by Provider's willful misconduct or gross negligence.

9. Updates and termination. Provider may update the Software or stop distributing it; an updated version is governed by the agreement included with it. Your rights end automatically if you breach this agreement. You may end it at any time by removing the Software.

10. Governing law. This agreement is governed by the laws of the Republic of Korea.

